{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-command plant, then layer compact specifications that: (i) bind clear sensing to forward-biased exploration, (ii) route each obstacle outcome through a dedicated recovery state with exactly one safe controllable, (iii) make backward motion rare and only front-obstacle-triggered, (iv) reserve full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort state after repeated front blockage, and (v) prevent repeated turning/random-walk/full-rotate so coverage returns quickly to forward motion.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception (uncontrollable obstacle/path events) from actuation (controllable motion pulses) in plant automata.",
    "Use one-shot recovery states in specifications so obstacle events preempt exploration, but noncritical path_clear usually does not preempt an already chosen recovery pulse.",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, allow occasional random_walk, and forbid steady turning-in-place as exploration.",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently.",
    "Handle obstacle_front through a short escalation chain: first directed turn, then brief backward escape if front remains blocked, then opposite turn, and only then last-resort full_rotate.",
    "After any successful recovery indication (especially path_clear), return immediately to forward-progress states."
  ],
